<title>CHINA: SUWA INT'L YEARLY NET RETURNS TO PROFIT.</title>
<headline>SUWA INT'L YEARLY NET RETURNS TO PROFIT.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   1.73 gain   vs 4.29 loss</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	   vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  4.42 gain   vs 28.16 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    8.06 profit vs 19.31 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		     559.05	vs 510.16</p>
<p>    Company name		 Suwa International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 16-23</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Suwa International is a computer component maker.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one 1999 warrant for every five shares held. The warrants are expected to be issued on October 15, 1997 to October 15, 1999 at the price of HK$0.60 per share.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on disposal of investment properties.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is one H.K. cent (including interim dividend of one cent) vs nil.</p>
<p>-- HK newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
